mber}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/deployments","created_at":"2018-04-16T08:34:38Z","updated_at":"2025-12-10T15:00:44Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T01:53:22Z","git_url":"git://github.com/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:zooniverse/front-end-monorepo.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo","homepage":"https://www.zooniverse.org","size":56586,"stargazers_count":109,"watchers_count":109,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":27,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":246,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["hacktoberfest","zooniverse"],"visibility":"public","forks":27,"open_issues":246,"watchers":109,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/pulls/3571","html_url":"https://github.com/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/pull/3571","diff_url":"https://github.com/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/pull/3571.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/pull/3571.patch","merged_at":"2022-09-06T15:52:42Z"},"body":"## Package\r\napp-project\r\napp-content-pages\r\n\r\n## Linked Issue and/or Talk Post\r\nhttps://github.com/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/pull/3529\r\n\r\n## Describe your changes\r\n\r\n### Linting\r\nMost changes in this PR are related to linter errors that prevent successful NextJS builds. I refactored the necessary components so that `useContext()` is not run conditionally, and `children` should no longer be passed as props.\r\n\r\n### Tests\r\n\r\nSeveral unit tests were updated for clarity of naming mocked stores.\r\n\r\n### Middleware\r\n\r\nNextJS 12.2 is supposed to have stable middleware, but our current implementation of middleware interferes with `router.query` after client-side navigation. In several components, we rely on `useRouter()` and then deconstruct `{ owner, project } = router.query`. However, in NextJS 12.2 `router.query` is an empty object after client-side navigation to home, /about, or /classify. Similar issue: https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/38528.\r\n\r\nI've deleted the middleware function for now. app-project's middleware was designed for a very specific use case to convert a `language` url param to a subpath, and legacy links to FEM projects that include a `language` param are rare enough that I'd rather address a middleware refactor in a future PR.\r\n\r\n\r\n### fetchStatuses() helper\r\n\r\nWhen running app-project `yarn test`, SubjectPicker > helpers > fetchStatuses() was throwing error from babel: Couldn't find a Program. Changing the function `updateSeenStatus()` inside of `fetchStatuses()` to an arrow function solved the error.\r\n\r\n## How to Review\r\n\r\nThe General UX checklist below is a good guide for this maintenance PR. Most components that were edited can be found in i-fancy-cats.\r\n\r\nI plan to follow up with another PR that unifies the naming of mocked stores in components with `useStores()`.\r\n\r\n# Checklist\r\n_PR Creator - Please cater the checklist to fit the review needed for your code changes._\r\n_PR Reviewer - Use the checklist during your review. Each point should be checkmarked or discussed before PR approval._\r\n\r\n## General\r\n- [x] Tests are passing locally and on Github\r\n- [x] Documentation is up to date and changelog has been updated if appropriate\r\n- [x] You can `yarn panic && yarn bootstrap` or `docker-compose up --build` and FEM works as expected\r\n- [ ] FEM works in all major desktop browsers: Firefox, Chrome, Edge, Safari (Use Browserstack account as needed)\r\n- [ ] FEM works in a mobile browser\r\n\r\n## General UX\r\nExample Staging Project: [i-fancy-cats](https://local.zooniverse.org:3000/projects/brooke/i-fancy-cats)\r\n- [x] All pages of a FEM project load: Home Page, Classify Page, and About Pages\r\n- [x] Can submit a classification\r\n- [x] Can sign-in and sign-out\r\n- [ ] The component is accessible\r\n  - Can be used with a screen reader [BBC guide to VoiceOver](https://bbc.github.io/accessibility-news-and-you/assistive-technology/testing-steps/voiceover-mac.html)\r\n  - Can be used from the keyboard [WebAIM guide to keyboard testing](https://webaim.org/techniques/keyboard/#testing)\r\n  - It is passing accessibility checks in the storybook\r\n\r\n## Refactoring\r\n- [x] The PR creator has described the reason for refactoring\r\n- [x] The refactored component(s) continue to work as expected\r\n\r\n## Maintenance\r\n- [x] If not from dependabot, the PR creator has described the update (major, minor, or patch version, changelog)\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/issues/3571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zooniverse/front-end-monorepo/issues/3571/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/1240820112","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/38528#issuecomment-1240820112","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/38528","id":1240820112,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBC3Cis5J9WmQ","user":{"login":"samuelcole","id":18301,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzAx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcole","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcole","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcole/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcole/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcole/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcole/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcole/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcole/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcole/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcole/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcole/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-09-08T14:46:14Z","updated_at":"2022-09-08T14:46:14Z","body":"I think this might be what I'm seeing! I walked through the code and found that 12.1.7 introduced some logic that removed the query params, and downgrading to 12.1.6 